,title,link,text,language,family
0,Ngardi - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ngardi,"May 2, 2025 - The Ngardi, also spelled Ngarti, are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Northern Territory and Western Australia.",Ngardi,Australian
1,Ngardi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ngardi_language,"October 15, 2024 - Ngardi, also spelt Ngarti or Ngardilj, is an Australian Aboriginal language that is considered moribund. It was previously thought to be an alternative name for the Bunara language, but these are now classified as separate languages.",Ngardi,Australian
2,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"June 4, 2026 - The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music forms a significant part of the unique heritage of a 40,000- to 60,000-year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo.",Ngardi,Australian
3,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"1 week ago - The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and musical instrumentation that are unique to particular regions or Aboriginal Australian groups; and some elements of musical tradition are common or widespread through much of the Australian continent, and even beyond.",Ngardi,Australian
4,Australian folk music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_folk_music,"July 18, 2025 - Australian folk music is the traditional music from the large variety of immigrant cultures and those of the original Australian inhabitants. Celtic, English, German and Scandinavian folk traditions predominated in the first wave of European immigrant music. The Australian tradition is, in ...",Ngardi,Australian
5,Australian Music prize: 80-year-old Kankawa Nagarra wins over Nick Cave and Amyl and the Sniffers | Australian music | The Guardian,https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/dec/04/australian-music-prize-2024-winner-kankawa-nagarra-wirlmarni,"December 4, 2024 - The Walmatjarri elder and blues musician Kankawa Nagarra has won the $50,000 Australian Music prize (AMP) for her debut album Wirlmarni, seeing off competition from Nick Cave, the Dirty Three and Amyl and the Sniffers.",Ngardi,Australian
6,Kankawa Nagarra Wins 20th Soundmerch Australian Music Prize for ‘Wirlarni’,https://www.billboard.com/music/awards/kankawa-nagarra-wins-20th-soundmerch-australian-music-prize-1235844248/,"December 4, 2024 - Kankawa Nagarra, the Queen of the Bandaral Ngadu and a Walmatjarri Elder, has been named the winner of the 20th Soundmerch Australian Music Prize (AMP) for her debut album Wirlmarni.",Ngardi,Australian
7,Music Makers: Sounds of Australia | Australian National Academy of Music,https://anam.com.au/anam-blog/music-makers-sounds-of-australia,"To start ANAM’s year, composer and academic Professor Christopher Sainsbury (b. 1963) gave an insightful keynote address to our musicians. Sainsbury founded the Ngarra-Burria First Nations composition program, and published his thoughts on this very question in his position paper, ‘New Music and the Search for an Australian Sound’ (Currency House, 2019).",Ngardi,Australian
8,Did you know Ngardi is severely endangered?,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/5246,Information from: “Austlang: Australian Indigenous Languages Database” .,Ngardi,Australian
9,Australia – The Rough Guide to World Music | Songlines,https://www.songlines.co.uk/the-rough-guide-to-world-music/the-rough-guide-to-world-music-australia,The story of Aboriginal music is centuries old and continues to develop in fascinating ways,Ngardi,Australian
